--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Notes on scope
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT license above covers this whole repository (punchstrip: the mabiicco MCP bridge in src-bridge/ and
test-bridge/, the mabi-ear MCP server in analysis/, the launchers, examples, build file and documents), except the
third-party files listed in NOTICE, which keep their own licenses.

MabiIcco itself is NOT part of this repository. punchstrip contains none of MabiIcco's code and works only with an
installed MabiIcco. MabiIcco / mmlTools is the work of its author, たんらる (https://github.com/fourthline/mmlTools);
MabiIcco, its binaries (MabiIcco.jar and the libraries shipped with it) and the Mabinogi game's sound files (DLS) are
not distributed here and belong to their respective owners.

Files that follow MabiIcco's own behaviour

Three source files re-implement parts of MabiIcco's behaviour so that the bridge, which runs without MabiIcco's
window, gives the same results as the application. Those portions follow the work of MabiIcco's author, たんらる
(https://github.com/fourthline/mmlTools); they are credited here and remain the author's work:

- src-bridge/mabibridge/render/OfflineRenderer.java
    the channel set-up of the application's synthesizer start-up (initializeSynthesizer: program change, CC91,
    CC64) and its per-track control (updateMidiControl: pan, volume, program change)
- src-bridge/mabibridge/engine/InstrumentTable.java
    the calculation of InstClass.logicalProgramNum(bank, program)
- src-bridge/mabibridge/engine/BridgeEngine.java
    the application's default static settings (optimizer level, MML options, the tempoAllowChordPart rule)

All other files call MabiIcco through its public classes at run time, from the user's own MabiIcco install, without
copying its code.
